.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt HEALTH 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm health
.Nd how this generation came to be running
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the release, this boot, how the previous generation ended, the
configuration files the SSH server started from, and the size of each log:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
release: dev
boot: 7c0e2b6a9d4f41e3a2b5c8d9e0f1a2b3, up 0 days 00:12:34 (754434 ticks)
recovery: previous=ended streak=0 seq=12
config: network from /etc/network.conf
config: sshd built-in defaults (no /etc/sshd.conf)
logs: fsd 2140 bytes, fsd.0 none, sshd 9812 bytes, sshd.0 none
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "recovery"
.It release
the release the file server serves
.Pq Xr release 1 .
.It boot
the kernel's boot identity and the boot tick counter, as
.Xr uptime 1
prints them.
.It recovery
how the previous generation of services ended, as the file server recorded
it for this boot before serving anything: its
.Li FSD RECOVERY
line in
.Pa /var/log/fsd
(or
.Pa /var/log/fsd.0
after a rotation) following this boot's
.Li started: boot
line.
.Ar previous
is
.Li none
(the first boot of this disk),
.Li ended
(an orderly
.Xr shutdown 8
or
.Xr reboot 8 ) ,
.Li failed
(the services were serving and the generation ended any other way), or
.Li not_ready
(the generation ended before the SSH server listened).
.Ar streak
counts failed generations in a row; the machine stops resetting itself when
it reaches its budget
.Pq Xr afterboot 8 .
.Ar seq
numbers the generations of this disk.
Only this boot's line is read: when it is not in either log (rotated out
or dropped), the line says
.Li unknown
and why.
Why a failed generation failed is printed on the console only;
.Nm
does not say.
.It config
whether the SSH server read each configuration file or used its built-in
defaults.
Sessions cannot change
.Pa /etc
and a malformed file stops the server from starting, so these are the
files the running server uses
.Pq Xr network.conf 5 , Xr sshd.conf 5 .
.It logs
the size of each log under
.Pa /var/log ,
or
.Li none .
.El
.Pp
.Fl Fl json
prints one bounded
.Li absd.observation_health.v1
JSON document with exactly four facts: boot identity, boot ticks, served
release, and this boot's retained recovery summary. Counters are decimal
strings; unavailable facts carry a reason and a null value. The document
does not include configuration, log sizes, a process census or fault causes.
Implementation identity stays unknown. A retained recovery record is not a
promise of the current server's process identity or latest restart.
.Pp
.Li recovery_not_retained
also covers a session without a mounted
.Pa /var/log ;
it does not distinguish a missing mount from an expired record.
.Pp
The payload is bounded to 8192 bytes. File-server requests can still stall;
the payload bound is not a command deadline. Remote acquisition needs its
own timeout and must treat no response as unavailable.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when every line was answered; 1 when a source refused or the recovery
line is unknown, in which case that line says why; 2 for a usage error.
.Pp
With
.Fl Fl json ,
0 means all four facts are known; 1 means a partial result; 2 means usage,
invalid acquisition interval or output failure. Configuration or log-size
errors can make human mode return 1 while the four JSON facts are complete.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr net-status 1 ,
.Xr sysinfo 1 ,
.Xr uptime 1 ,
.Xr afterboot 8
